From 9c64a50e995553085830bbf98a761032c5dfc788 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: linux-a9 <linux-a9@localhost>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:30:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soc: apple: add opt-in fingerprinted A9 AOP running attach

An inherited AOP with an empty outbox previously stopped before any protocol
exchange. Verify the running image windows and loader tags against pinned
20H350 firmware, then require its intact external segment to be in a
boot-time reservation Linux cannot recycle before allowing mailbox traffic.

Require two consecutive seq/seq+1 ping acknowledgments within three bounded
probes. Share the observer's immutable attach parameter, and require active=1
as well before sending exactly one HELLO_REPLY. Adopt only after EPMAP and
reuse normal endpoint, ring, calibration and IIO bring-up. Refuse all other
responses without retries or inherited-state writes, warn loudly about zombie
firmware and preserve that refusal at shutdown. Also accept seq+1 in the
ordinary cold-path ping watchdog. Record proof flags and transaction phases.

The firmware response and ownership interpretation remain unverified on the
device. Offline ASan/UBSan policy/parser tests and W=1 AOP object builds pass.
---
